/** @defgroup midistreamplayer_management MidiStreamPlayer
 *  @brief Real-time MIDI event playback for interactive, gameplay, and procedural music systems.
 *
 *  @details
 *  MidiStreamPlayer is the live-event playback MIDI message component in Maestro MPTK.
 *  Instead of loading a complete MIDI file, your code creates and sends events at runtime.
 *  For setup guidance and news, see https://paxstellar.fr/midi-file-player-detailed-view-2-2/
 *
 *  @par Typical scenarios
 *  - interactive instruments and keyboard input,
 *  - gameplay-driven musical responses,
 *  - generative/procedural music systems,
 *  - runtime control of pitch wheel, channels, and chords.
 *
 *  MidiStreamPlayer inherits from MidiSynth, so synthesis and channel features
 *  from MidiSynth remain available.
 *
 *  Recommended reading order:
 *  1. @ref midistreamplayer_overview
 *  2. @ref midistreamplayer_realtime
 *  3. @ref mptkevent_concept
 *  4. @ref midistreamplayer_chords
 *  5. @ref midistreamplayer_pro
 *
 *  @see @ref midistreamplayer_overview
 *  @see @ref midistreamplayer_realtime
 *  @see @ref mptkevent_concept
 *  @see @ref midistreamplayer_chords
 *  @see @ref midistreamplayer_pro
 */

